    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`). There's only one test class in the project (`AcceptanceTest`), and both it and the whole build pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature on the owner endpoints. The request may carry an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and the owner's `salutation` is returned as `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges, following the existing OpenAPI-driven Spring conventions:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n   - Added an optional `title` string to the `OwnerFields` (input) schema.\n   - Added a read-only derived `salutation` string to the `Owner` (output) schema.\n   (DTOs are generated from this spec at build time.)\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter, so the value survives create \u2192 read.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `salutation(owner)` derivation method and wired it into `toOwnerDto` via `@Mapping`. MapStruct auto-maps the incoming `title` from `OwnerFieldsDto` to the `Owner` model (same-named String). The method treats absent/blank titles as \"no title\" and returns just the last name.\n\n4. **`src/main/resources/db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table. The test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to exist in DDL for the persisted title to round-trip.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (POST `title=DR`, `lastName=who` \u2192 GET `$.salutation == \"DR who\"`) passes.",
